invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma.c
catches: rsa_ifma_model_test_384
reason: The switch's case for eight registers passes a where b belongs,
  so a modulus of 46 to 51 words, RSA-3072 among them, gets a squared in
  place of a times b. It compiles with no warning, because the other
  cases still read b. A server object compiles the kernel at the 384-byte
  bound, and bin/rsa_ifma_model_test_384 runs that build over the lane
  model and compares rsa_vp1_cpu under the bit with rsa_vp1.

--- old
    case 8:
        almost_montgomery_product_8(out, a, b, modulus);
--- new
    case 8:
        almost_montgomery_product_8(out, a, a, modulus);
